# Home Assistant repository context

This project is a **Home Assistant configuration** git repo (YAML, automations, integrations).

## When to load `repo-docs/`

At the **start** of a turn, if the task involves any of the following, **read** `repo-docs/HA_DIAGNOSTICS.md` from the workspace root (read tool) **before** proposing fixes, unless the user attached it or the file is already in context:

- Integrations, entities, logs, or errors (`home-assistant.log`, MCP `get_error_log`, etc.)
- Proxmox VE, Jellyfin, Imou, IEC, or similar integrations mentioned in that doc
- “Why is X broken?” / diagnostics / health of this HA instance

## If not applicable

Skip the read for purely mechanical edits (typo, rename, unrelated file) with no HA troubleshooting angle.

## After reading

Prefer updating `repo-docs/HA_DIAGNOSTICS.md` when you discover new durable findings (symptoms, MCP counts, fixes applied, operational steps).
